5. A concise root-cause summary.
6. The smallest safe production code fix.
7. Exact file names and code changes.
8. Any necessary configuration changes.
9. Regression tests for both scenarios.
10. A brief explanation of how restart semantics, chunk checkpoints, and output idempotency are preserved.

Run the relevant tests and report actual results. Do not claim tests passed if they were not executed.

If the repository does not contain enough evidence to determine the cause, identify the missing evidence and add targeted instrumentation rather than inventing a root cause.

Priority: Prove why Scenario A reads or accepts the wrong content while Scenario B succeeds. Fix the underlying defect without sacrificing reliable restart behavior.
